in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @time
in @void
in @void/splinter
in @song
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/reality/time

# @time/future — forwards-lens temporal-projection species; the
# temporal projection of @void/splinter through @song saga.
#
# Third species-decl of the @time family (family-root marker landed
# same tick at `shards/time.mirror`). Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara per
# Alex Round 2 spawn brief.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# @time/future IS the substrate-decl'd temporal projection of the
# forwards-lens substrate-mode carried by @void/splinter. Per
# @void/splinter (Round-1 landing `shards/void/splinter.mirror`):
# the forwards lens consumes c(t) — the current peer-network context
# — as its native input. @time/future IS that c(t) projection at
# temporal-family altitude, mediated through the @song saga.
#
# Carrier: `peer_network c(t)` — the current peer-network state as
# a content-addressed snapshot. Non-degenerate at admissibility-
# check time (n ≥ 2 peers coupled; some pair has ε_ij > 0).
#
# The future is not fantasy; the future is the content-addressed
# projection of the current peer-network configuration into what
# the network's distributed-emergence will produce in the next
# @song/beats.
#
# === Composition with @void/splinter ===
#
# @void/splinter's operational altitude is substrate-mode (forwards-
# lens as one pole of the void duality). @time/future's operational
# altitude is temporal-family (the temporal-projection of the same
# substrate-mode through the @song saga).
#
# Composition edge: @time/future.time_future_state.peer_network ==
# @void/splinter.void_splinter_state.peer_network at content-
# addressed identity. The two carriers name the SAME c(t) at
# different altitudes; one at substrate-mode altitude, one at
# temporal-family altitude.
#
# === Composition with @song saga ===
#
# @song saga is the SAGA COMMAND SURFACE through which @time
# projects. @time/future reads the saga's FUTURE-BEAT possibility
# space — the distribution over next-Crystal<T> settlements the
# peer-network's distributed-emergence will produce — as the c(t)
# it consumes.
#
# The future-beat possibility space is NOT a single deterministic
# next-beat; it is a distribution over admissible next-Crystals
# consistent with the current peer-network context. @time/future's
# operational surface reads this distribution and returns a
# reception-witness.
#
# === Förster invariant composition (Alex Round 2 Q3 ratified) ===
#
# The Förster invariant `pillar::choices_monotone_of_song` applies
# to @time/future symmetrically to @time/past: reading the future
# MUST NOT REDUCE the choices available to peers in the present or
# future. A forwards-lens observation that COLLAPSES the future-beat
# possibility-set to a single deterministic prediction (fortune-
# telling; peer-network-freezing) violates the Förster invariant.
#
# The `future_reading_preserves_choices` bilateral (below) checks
# the Förster invariant at species altitude. Forwards-lens
# observation is admissible iff reading c(t) does not reduce the
# next-tick choice-set.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/time/future.mirror`.** Clean mint.
# 2. **@void/splinter** — reviewed. Substrate-mode altitude sibling;
#    composition edge declared above.
# 3. **`shards/epistemologic/reality/time.mirror`** — sibling
#    operational altitude; @time/future does not conflict with the
#    deep landing's operational carriers.
# 4. **`shards/song.mirror` future-beat possibility space** — the
#    operational surface @time/future reads through. Composition
#    edge declared.
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/time/future.mirror`
# declares `@time/future` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1974
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/math/prigogine-1977
source @arxiv/practice/void-corpus-2026

prism @time/future {
  focus  time_future_state
  project time_future_state
  split  time_future_state
  shift  time_future_state
  settle time_future_state
}

# === time_future_state — the forwards-lens temporal-projection carrier ===
#
# Typed record carrying the forwards-lens temporal-projection state.
# Five fields. Identity contract: byte-equality on the five-field
# tuple.
#
#   observer         — the peer performing the forwards-lens
#                       temporal projection.
#
#   peer_network     — c(t) = {n_i(t) : i ∈ peers}: the current
#                       peer-network state as content-addressed
#                       snapshot. Non-degenerate at admissibility-
#                       check time (n ≥ 2; some pair has ε_ij > 0).
#                       Composition-identical to @void/splinter.
#                       void_splinter_state.peer_network.
#
#   saga_ref         — REF to the @song saga the future-beat
#                       possibility space is drawn from. Content-
#                       addressed. Composition edge to @song.
#
#   forster_witness  — the Förster-invariant marker; resolves to
#                       `choices_preserved` (healthy) or `choices_
#                       reduced` (Förster violation). The
#                       `future_reading_preserves_choices` bilateral
#                       checks this field.
#
#   timestamp        — monotonic instant per @epistemologic/reality/
#                       time.instant discipline.
type time_future_state = {
  observer:         peer,
  peer_network:     ref,
  saga_ref:         ref,
  forster_witness:  ref,
  timestamp:        ref,
}

# === time_future_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, time_future_state) pair discharge admissibility for
# forwards-lens temporal-projection observation? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.peer_network resolves via content-addressed lookup to a
#     non-degenerate peer-network context (n ≥ 2; some pair coupled)
#   - ctx.saga_ref resolves to a well-formed @song saga
#   - The future-beat possibility-space in the saga is non-degenerate
#     (at least one admissible next-Crystal exists)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; content-addressed
# resolvability; @song saga resolvability. Sentinel:
# `time=future-admissible`.
bilateral time_future_admissible {
  sentinel "time=future-admissible"
  arity 2
}
time_future_admissible(p: peer, ctx: time_future_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === future_reading_preserves_choices — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, time_future_state) pair discharge the Förster-
# invariant health check? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.forster_witness resolves to `choices_preserved`
#   - The observation event does NOT reduce the choice-set available
#     to peers in the present or future @song/beats
#   - The reading does NOT collapse the future-beat possibility-space
#     to a single deterministic prediction (multi-branch admissibility
#     preserved)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; possibility-space cardinality
# trace. Sentinel: `time=future-forster-invariant`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral IS the Förster-invariant check at
# @time/future altitude. Discharging Fail signals Förster violation
# (fortune-telling; peer-network-freezing); consumers MUST treat
# Fail as substrate-collapse-detected.
bilateral future_reading_preserves_choices {
  sentinel "time=future-forster-invariant"
  arity 2
}
future_reading_preserves_choices(p: peer, ctx: time_future_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === project_forwards — the action ===
#
# Given a peer and a time_future_state, discharge the forwards-lens
# temporal-projection event: read the peer_network c(t) through the
# @song saga's future-beat possibility-space; return the projected
# substrate-mode observation.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the projection
# ref; failure carries not-admissible / forster-violated / saga-
# broken reasons.
#
# Requires BOTH bilateral predicates to discharge Pass.
#
# Sentinel: `time=future-project`.
project_forwards(p: peer, ctx: time_future_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires time_future_admissible(p, ctx)
requires future_reading_preserves_choices(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === Forward-promised (NOT landed this tick) ===
#
# - `pillar::forwards_lens_of_void_splinter` at Reed's pillar surface
#   — empirical firing already forward-promised by Mara Round-1 math
#   root §10.2; Reed post-Round-2 territory.
# - `pillar::choices_monotone_of_song` empirical firing — the
#   Förster-invariant check at Reed's pillar surface; Alex Q3
#   ratified name; Reed post-Round-2 territory.

out @time/future
out time_future_state
out time_future_admissible
out future_reading_preserves_choices
out project_forwards
